4. Routes (routes/web.php)

Public:
Method   URI                Action                              Name
GET      /                  closure → welcome
GET      /page/{slug}       PageController@show                 pages.show
GET      /posts             PostController@publicIndex          posts.index
GET      /posts/{slug}      PostController@publicShow           posts.show
GET      /category/{slug}   PostController@publicByCategory     categories.show

Admin (group: middleware('auth'), prefix('admin'), name('admin.')):
- Route::resource('pages', PageController::class)
- Route::post('posts/upload-image', PostController@uploadImage)->name('posts.upload_image')
- Route::get('posts/drafts', PostController@drafts)->name('posts.drafts')
- Route::patch('posts/{post}/toggle', PostController@togglePublish)->name('posts.toggle')
- Route::resource('posts', PostController::class)
- Route::resource('categories', CategoryController::class)
- Route::get('/menu', MenuItemController@index)->name('menu.index')
- Route::post('/menu', MenuItemController@store)->name('menu.store')
- Route::put('/menu/{menuItem}', MenuItemController@update)->name('menu.update')
- Route::delete('/menu/{menuItem}', MenuItemController@destroy)->name('menu.destroy')
- Route::get('/settings', SettingController@index)->name('settings.index')
- Route::put('/settings', SettingController@update)->name('settings.update')

Breeze:
- GET /dashboard → redirect to admin.pages.index
- /profile — edit/update/destroy
- /auth/* — from routes/auth.php

5. Data model

Model      Table         Columns used by app                                    Notes
Page       pages         title, slug, content, is_published, is_admin_only     casts booleans
Post       posts         title, slug, body, is_published, image_path, category_id   slug unique, nullable
Category   categories    name, slug                                             hasMany posts
MenuItem   menu_items    title, url, page_id, parent_id, order                  belongsTo Page; belongsTo self (parent); hasMany self (children)
Setting    settings      key, value                                             key-value store
User       users         standard Breeze

Important:
- Post uses `body` for content (not `content`). slug is stored and unique — PostController::store()/update() compute it from title.
- MenuItem: parent_id is nullable FK to menu_items.id, ON DELETE SET NULL. Deleting a parent promotes its children to top level.
- MenuItem::order is per-sibling-group ordering (applied via children() relation). Top-level items also ordered by `order`.
- MenuItem::getTargetUrlAttribute() computes target_url from page_id (via routes) or url, falling back to '#'.

Public URL note: PostController::publicShow($slug) fetches all posts and matches slug (fallback: computes slug from title if the column is empty). Slow at scale — see §14.

6. Layouts

Two parallel layouts. Each is used by a distinct set of pages. Do not mix them.

layouts/admin.blade.php
- Used by @extends('layouts.admin') + @section('content')
- Contains an @php block reading $globalSettings (or querying Setting::pluck)
- @include('partials.theme-vars') renders CSS variables and body/heading styling
- @include('layouts.navigation'), then @yield('content'), then @stack('scripts')
- Contains CKEditor content styling and admin-panel-specific CSS

layouts/app.blade.php
- Used via <x-app-layout> component (App\View\Components\AppLayout)
- Same @php block, same partial include
- Uses {{ $slot }} — not @yield('content')
- Has @isset($header) block for named header slot

Rule: any blade using <x-app-layout> must pass content as a slot. Any blade using @extends('layouts.app') + @section('content') will render blank, because there is no @yield('content') in that layout. Use <x-app-layout> or switch to @extends('layouts.admin').

layouts/navigation.blade.php
- Shared nav. Uses $globalSettings for site name and header styling, and $headerMenuItems for the dynamic menu (set by AppServiceProvider).
- $headerMenuItems is now a tree (top-level items with `children` set recursively), NOT a flat collection.
- Desktop: @include('partials.menu-item', ['item' => $item]) — each top-level item is passed to the partial.
- Mobile: @include('partials.menu-item-mobile', ['item' => $item, 'depth' => 0]).
- Admin-only filtering moved into AppServiceProvider (before tree build), so the blade no longer filters.

partials/theme-vars.blade.php
- Contains raw CSS (no <style> wrapper) that outputs the CSS variables and applies them to body, headings, and .bg-primary/.text-primary/button[type="submit"] etc. Included inside the <style> block of both layouts.

partials/menu-item.blade.php
- Top-level desktop nav item. If the item has children, renders a wrapper `<div class="relative h-full flex items-center" x-data="{ open: false }">` with hover/focus handling, a chevron toggle button (for touch), and an absolutely-positioned dropdown containing @include('partials.menu-item-dropdown') for each child. If no children, renders a plain <x-nav-link>.
- Parent renders as link + chevron if it has url/page_id, as button + chevron otherwise.

partials/menu-item-dropdown.blade.php
- Recursive: items inside a dropdown. If the item has children, opens a submenu to the right on hover. If no children, renders as a simple <a>.

partials/menu-item-mobile.blade.php
- Recursive: mobile hamburger items. Indented via inline style padding-left: {{ 16 + ($depth * 16) }}px (Tailwind JIT can't see dynamically-built class names). Tap-to-expand for items with children; plain <a> for leaves.

7. CKEditor 5 setup

Installation
npm install ckeditor5 @ckeditor/ckeditor5-style @ckeditor/ckeditor5-font \
  @ckeditor/ckeditor5-alignment @ckeditor/ckeditor5-highlight \
  @ckeditor/ckeditor5-list @ckeditor/ckeditor5-source-editing \
  @ckeditor/ckeditor5-show-blocks
All GPL-licensed. No premium packages.

Initializer — resources/js/ckeditor-init.js
- First two lines (essential): import 'ckeditor5/ckeditor5.css'; import 'ckeditor5/ckeditor5-content.css';
- licenseKey: 'GPL'
- Exposes window.initCkEditor(selector, options)
- Merges options.simpleUpload for image uploads
- Attaches a form submit listener that syncs editor content back into the <textarea>

Blade pattern (four files)
@push('scripts')
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/build/assets/ckeditor-init-<HASH>.css">
<script type="module">
    import('{{ Vite::asset("resources/js/ckeditor-init.js") }}').then(() => {
        window.initCkEditor('#body', {
            simpleUpload: {
                uploadUrl: '{{ route("admin.posts.upload_image") }}',
                headers: { 'X-CSRF-TOKEN': '{{ csrf_token() }}' }
            }
        }).catch(err => console.error('[CKEditor] init failed', err));
    }).catch(err => console.error('[CKEditor] module load failed', err));
</script>
@endpush

Field targets:
admin/pages/create.blade.php   #content
admin/pages/edit.blade.php     #content
admin/posts/create.blade.php   #body
admin/posts/edit.blade.php     #body

Why <link> plus dynamic import()
- Vite splits dynamically imported modules into separate JS and CSS chunks. Loading only the JS leaves the CSS unloaded, and the editor renders with oversized unstyled icons. The explicit <link> on the CSS chunk fixes it.

The <link> hash changes on every npm run build. After a rebuild, update the hash in all four blades:

$manifest = Get-Content public\build\manifest.json -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json
$css = "/build/" + $manifest.'resources/js/ckeditor-init.js'.css[0]
$blades = "resources\views\admin\pages\create.blade.php","resources\views\admin\pages\edit.blade.php","resources\views\admin\posts\create.blade.php","resources\views\admin\posts\edit.blade.php"
foreach ($f in $blades) {
    $c = Get-Content $f -Raw
    $c = $c -replace '/build/assets/ckeditor-init-[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\.css', $css
    [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText((Resolve-Path $f), $c, (New-Object System.Text.UTF8Encoding $false))
}
php artisan view:clear

vite.config.js
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
import laravel from 'laravel-vite-plugin';

export default defineConfig({
    plugins: [
        laravel({
            input: [
                'resources/css/app.css',
                'resources/js/app.js',
                'resources/js/ckeditor-init.js'
            ],
            refresh: true,
        }),
    ],
    optimizeDeps: { include: ['ckeditor5'] },
    build: { commonjsOptions: { include: [/ckeditor5/, /node_modules/] } },
});

8. Theme / settings system

Settings page: admin/settings/index.blade.php. Form posts to PUT admin.settings.update.
Fields:
- settings[site_name] — string
- settings[primary_color] — native color input, default #2563eb
- settings[accent_color] — default #f59e0b
- settings[text_color] — default #1f2937
- settings[header_bg_color] — default #ffffff
- settings[heading_font], settings[body_font], settings[border_radius], settings[container_width] — dropdowns
- header_image — file upload
- remove_header_image — checkbox

How theming works:
- Settings stored in settings table (key / value).
- Both layouts read $globalSettings and @include('partials.theme-vars').
- The partial outputs CSS variables (--primary-color, --accent-color, --text-color, --heading-font, --body-font, --border-radius) and rules for body, headings, and button[type="submit"]/.btn-primary.
- tailwind.config.js maps classes to variables:
  - gray.700, gray.900 → var(--text-color)
  - blue.500, blue.600, blue.700 → var(--primary-color)
  - indigo.500, indigo.600, indigo.700 → var(--primary-color)
  - amber.500, amber.600 → var(--accent-color)

What responds to settings:
- text_color → body copy and headings, and every text-gray-700 / text-gray-900 / bg-gray-700 / bg-gray-900 element
- primary_color → every bg-blue-600, text-blue-600, bg-indigo-600, text-indigo-600, hover:bg-blue-700, etc. Also button[type="submit"] on admin
- accent_color → amber-500/amber-600 classes
- heading_font, body_font → applied to body and h1..h6
- header_bg_color → used directly in layouts/navigation.blade.php

What does NOT respond: border_radius, container_width.

9. AppServiceProvider

Shares two variables with all views via View::composer('*', ...):
- $globalSettings — array of all settings (Setting::pluck('value', 'key'))
- $headerMenuItems — tree of menu items, top-level only, with `children` eager-set recursively

Menu building:
- Fetches MenuItem::with('page')->orderBy('order')->get()
- If user is not authenticated, rejects items whose page->is_admin_only is true — before building the tree, so descendants of a hidden node are hidden too.
- Calls MenuItem::buildTree($items) to produce the tree.

Both writes are guarded by Schema::hasTable() so a fresh install without migrations doesn't crash view rendering.

10. Menu feature (added this session)

Schema:
- menu_items.parent_id — nullable foreignId, constrained to menu_items.id, nullOnDelete, after('id')

Model (MenuItem):
- $fillable includes parent_id
- casts: page_id, parent_id, order → integer
- parent() — belongsTo self via parent_id
- children() — hasMany self via parent_id, orderBy('order')
- descendantIds() — flat array of all descendant ids, walks the loaded `children` relation
- buildTree(?Collection $items, ?int $parentId) — static, returns a collection of top-level items with `children` set recursively

Controller (MenuItemController):
- index() — fetches all items, builds tree, flattens to {item, depth} objects for the admin list, passes $flattened and $pages
- store() — validates title, page_id, url, order, parent_id; clears url if page_id set; creates
- update() — validates the same fields (all "sometimes"); rejects parent_id that is self or a descendant (cycle prevention); clears url if page_id set
- destroy() — sets children's parent_id to null (promote to top level), then deletes
- flatten(Collection $items, int $depth) — protected, recurses into children to produce {item, depth}

Admin UI (admin/menu/index.blade.php):
- Add form: Link Title, Parent (select), Link to Dynamic Page, Custom URL, Display Order
- List: each item shown with indentation (padding-left: depth * 24px) and a ↳ marker for nested items
- Each row has an Edit button that toggles an inline expandable form (Alpine x-data="{ editing: false }") containing all fields, and a Remove button
- The expanded form's Parent select excludes self and descendants
- On save, page reloads collapsed with a green flash

Frontend rendering:
- Top-level items → partials/menu-item.blade.php
- Items inside dropdowns → partials/menu-item-dropdown.blade.php (recursive)
- Mobile items → partials/menu-item-mobile.blade.php (recursive, inline padding for indentation)
- Behavior: hover-open on desktop with focus-within for keyboard; tap-toggle for touch; @click.away to close

