- All Breeze controllers, all Breeze components, bootstrap/app.php, config/*, remaining migrations

15. Where to start a future session

If the app is working and you're extending it: read the file you're about to modify, then modify it. Don't assume the pattern from another file.

If something is broken: paste the exact error, the file it points to, and any log output. That's usually enough to diagnose.

If you want to keep cleaning: the table in §13 lists what's left. None of it is urgent.

If you want to change how the menu system works: the flow is: admin/menu/index.blade.php (UI) → MenuItemController (validation + persistence) → MenuItem model (relations, buildTree, descendantIds) → AppServiceProvider (tree build + admin-only filter) → partials/menu-item*.blade.php (rendering).

If you want to change how the theme system works: settings page → partials/theme-vars.blade.php → tailwind.config.js.

16. If you start a new chat

Paste this report at the top. Then, if you're asking about a specific file, paste that file too. The combination gives the AI the project context and the specific content it needs to reason about — which is far better than asking it to guess from a description.

Also consider turning on any "reasoning" or "deep thinking" mode the interface offers. The project has enough internal contradictions that careful reasoning beats fast pattern-matching.

Critical: on this machine, any file you ask the AI to write should be handed over as a script that uses [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText(..., UTF8Encoding $false), not as content to paste into VS Code. Pasting into VS Code has silently failed four times in this project. Always verify after saving with Get-Item ... | Select-Object Length.